D direction: C's sophisticated dusk woodland atmosphere, material cohesion, painted lighting and environmental depth + B's crisp category silhouettes, calm center, controlled broad forms and immediately readable information. Do not split into two styles: ONE unified original artistic system.
Shared hero identity, identical in ALL D images: one living ivory fantasy snake, medium-small expressive almond amber eyes (not huge baby eyes), softly triangular elegant head with gently rounded short snout, subtle smile/alert gaze, moss-leaf brow. Head width only about1.3 times neck width; no bobblehead. Head, neck, muscular flexible body, long progressive taper and pointed fine tail are ONE anatomically continuous silhouette, same cream material and light throughout. Scale flow follows anatomy, selectively painted overlapping scales, not a repeated checkerboard/tile ribbon. Moss and foliage organically rooted in irregular asymmetrical growth islands, clumps follow curves; only2–3 tiny rust-red mushrooms across whole back, NEVER on head, no mushroom hat, no periodic identical per-segment attachments. No ears/horns/limbs. Shadows directional and consistent, no glued-on head. Personality survives small gameplay height.
D materials/light: cream/ivory highest foreground value, moss jade/olive with restrained honey rim light, dusk petrol/indigo woodland edge planes. One soft warm upper-left key and cool ambient bounce consistent across all surfaces. Detailed crafted materials but broad quiet value shapes first. Painted local illumination ONLY; no realtime blur look or full-screen bloom.
Strict visual hierarchy: Snake > active food/pickup > collision obstacle > interactive environment > decorative foliage > ground. Different silhouettes and materials, NOT just different colors.
Art VFX only authored organic leaves/spores/fungal dust and directional light wisps rooted in action/environment; no generic circular rings, geometric particles, laser halos, CSS glow, random clutter. All images conceptual only, no functioning mechanics/UI/backend.
Main Menu constraints: preserve information architecture and all features, no new mechanics/accounts/backends. One original integrated forest illustration; Snake hero inhabits same ground/light/world as menu, not cutout pasted on background. UI is bespoke botanical/wood/bronze world charms, quiet materials and deliberate readable typography, NOT HTML panels/dashboard rectangles, no nested brown windows. No source cropping.
